      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`qknorm_complex_rope` (the bit-exact RMSNorm + complex RoPE of Qwen-Image-2.1 attention prep) reaches about 3.2 TB/s on B200, half of what a plain copy of the same bytes does. Each half-warp loads one row, then waits on a reduction and the rotation before its store, so few bytes are in flight.\n\n## Modifications\n\nThe kernel now takes the Q/K rows two at a time per half-warp: both rows' loads are issued before either row is normalized and rotated. `norm_rope_row` is split into `load_row` and `norm_rope_store`; the arithmetic is the same code, so the output stays bit-identical. Prefix copies, V copies and an odd tail row keep the existing one-row loop. The launch uses half as many blocks.\n\nWider variants were measured and are not used: 256/512 threads per block (no gain, slower at 512), and 4 or 8 rows per half-warp through arrays (slower).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOutputs of the single-tensor and the pack entry points are `torch.equal` to the previous kernel at 4352 and 9216 tokens (24 heads x 128).\n\n- `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_qwen_image21_cuda.py`: 28 passed (B200).\n- `test/registered/kernels/ops/diffusion/test_complex_rope.py`: 43 passed (B200).\n- `test/registered/kernels/ops/diffusion/test_model_fast_paths.py -k \"qknorm or qwen\"`: 33 passed; `test_ernie_qknorm_rope_is_bit_exact` fails the same way on unmodified main and does not use this kernel.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nB200, Q+K through the pack entry point, 24 heads x 128, three alternating runs each:\n\n| tokens | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4352 | 33.0 / 33.0 / 32.9 us | 31.0 / 31.0 / 30.9 us (-6%) |\n| 9216 | 71.8 / 71.8 / 71.8 us | 65.3 / 65.4 / 65.2 us (-9%) |\n\nEnd to end this is small: Qwen-Image-2.1 1024px, 40 steps, one B200, two alternating runs each, 2.20 / 2.20 s before and 2.19 / 2.18 s after (about -0.4%).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41410753564](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41410753564)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41410753664](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41410753664)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41410753645](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41410753645)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
